#### 5. `models/user.js` - User Schema Definition
**Purpose**: Defines the structure for user data in MongoDB

**Schema Structure**:
```javascript
const userSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  name: String,                    // User's full name
  email: String,                   // Unique email address
  password: String,                 // Hashed password
  role: String,                     // 'patient', 'doctor', or 'admin'
  phone: String,                    // Phone number
  gender: String,                   // Gender information
  
  // Doctor-specific fields
  specialization: String,           // Medical specialization
  qualification: String,            // Medical qualifications
  experience: Number,               // Years of experience
  consultationFee: Number,         // Fee per consultation
  
  // Patient-specific fields
  age: Number,                      // Patient age
  bloodGroup: String,               // Blood group
  medicalHistory: [String],          // Medical conditions
  allergies: [String],               // Known allergies
  
  isNewPatient: Boolean,            // First-time visit flag
  totalVisits: Number,              // Total appointment count
  lastVisitDate: Date               // Last appointment date
});
```

